<h2><strong>What is Presidents&rsquo; Day?</strong>&nbsp;</h2>
<p>Presidents\' Day as a Washington\'s Birthday has a history as old as US country itself. It was started to celebrate publicly for the first time in the late 18th century, while George Washington was still president. Following the death of him in 1799, his
    birthday of February 22 became an important day of remembrance.</p>
